  What the frick?
  *I'm bold and brave*
  /I'm italian/
  _See me? Underlined_
** Tasks
  - ( ) Undone -> not done yet
  - (x) Done -> done with that
  - (?) Needs further input

  - (!) Urgent -> high priority task
  - (+) Recurring task with children

  - (-) Pending -> currently in progress
  - (=) Task put on hold
  - (_) Task cancelled (put down)

  ===
@code rust
/// A rust-codeblock inside norg
///
/// Will print "Hello, World!"
///
/// All the variables used here aren't needed.
/// The type annotation for the variables here are not needed.
/// A simpler "Hello, World!" (that will do the same):
/// ```rust main.rs
/// fn main() {
/// println!("Hello, World!")
/// }
/// ```
fn main() {
let mut hi: String = String::from("Hello");
let comma: &str = ", ";
hi += comma;
let planet = "World";
println!("{}{}!", hi, planet)
}
@end
